The '''Palace spire''', known as '''Temple Spire''' or the '''Tranquility Spire''' during the [[Republic Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]], was the highest spire built atop of the [[Imperial Palace]], formerly the [[Jedi]] [[Jedi temple|Temple]], on [[Coruscant]]. It was surrounded by four smaller spires collectively referred to as the [[Council Towers]].

==Description==
A towering spire with three decorative fins at its summit, Tranquility Spire protruded from the heart of the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] for a [[millennium]]. One of the [[Jedi Order]]'s holiest sites, its interior was lined with galleries depicting the Order's [[Timeline of galactic history|history]]. Mosaics, tapestries, and sculptures were suspended in the center of the tower, suspended on [[Repulsorlift|repulsors]] and were viewed through [[transparisteel]] [[turbolift]]s that lined the outer walls of the spire.<ref name="NoP" /> It was surrounded by four smaller spires collectively referred to as the [[Council Towers]].<ref name="NoP" /> At the base of the tower, the original [[mountain]] peak of the [[sacred spire]] jutted out of the ziggurat and was encircled by hallways which overlooked the barren slopes of the edifice. Pathways led from the outer halls onto the mountain and through it, leading down into original [[cave]] chapels. It was the site of [[meditation]] balconies and a [[Lower balcony (Sacred spire)|balcony]] that presented a series of [[Hologram|holo-depictions]] of the history of the [[Jedi]] where the [[Jedi Initiate|younglings]] were brought for education.<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> The Spire's apex contained halls and a chamber that was important to the Order, including private meditation and contemplation rooms, lecture halls, and a [[The galaxy|galaxy]] [[holomap]] room. The [[Republic Military|military]] command center of the Jedi was also located in this section of the [[Jedi temple|Temple]].<ref name="NoP" />

Within the finned portion of the Spire was the [[Veranda (Jedi Temple)|Veranda]], which housed the [[Hall of Knighthood]] and a private [[hangar]] for dignitaries as well as members of the [[Jedi High Council]]. The [[Pinnacle Room]] of the Spire housed the most important documents and artifacts of the Order; it was also used as a meeting place for the High Council in addition to the [[Jedi Council Chamber]].<ref name="NoP" />

After the [[Order 66|fall]] of the Jedi Order and subsequent [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Darth Sidious]] took up residence in the Jedi Temple, transforming the Temple Spire into the seat of government of the Empire. Converting the pinnacle chamber to his [[Emperor's throne room (Imperial Palace)|throne room]],<ref name="NoP" /> it was renamed the Palace spire<ref name="Tarkin" /> and the rest of the spire was stripped of all references to the once proud Jedi and in its place was installed statues and art dedicated to the glory of the Empire.<ref name="NoP" />

